//:: cases TC_LK_6_UnlockDeadFromLockedRegion
//:: tools silicon
//:: verdict Fail

// TC-LK-6: unlockDead fires due to dead code introduced INSIDE the locked region.
//
// The lock invariant (val > 0) is satisfiable, so:
//   lockInvariantUnsatisfiable — does NOT fire (invariant OK in isolation)
//   lockDead                   — does NOT fire (state is live when lock is reached)
//
// Inside the locked region, 'assume val < 0' contradicts the invariant fact val > 0,
// making the state dead.  DetectDeadCode fires deadBranch for the assume.
// The per-site Refute(ff)(UnlockDeadCodeBlame) at the end of the unlock expansion
// then fires unlockDead because the state is still dead when unlock is reached.
//
// This shows unlockDead is independent: it catches dead state that was
// introduced by arbitrary code inside the locked region, not just by the invariant.
lock_invariant Perm(val, write) ** val > 0;
class DeadInsideLockedRegion {
    int val;

    requires committed(this);
    void method() {
        lock this;
        // State: Perm(val,write) ** val > 0 — live.  lockDead does NOT fire.
        assume val < 0;
        // val > 0 ∧ val < 0 → false.  State is dead.
        // DetectDeadCode: deadBranch("code after assume val < 0") fires.
        unlock this;
        // unlockDead fires: dead state from inside the locked region
        // persists through fold / exhale / exhale in the unlock expansion.
    }
}
